; link/pop_scene.link — the SCENE's program, staged past the LOADM handover (P3.106).
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, WHICH IS A MEASUREMENT AND NOT A PREFERENCE.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The intro and the scene both linked at $2000 and were LOADM'd separately. Merged into
; one image they are
;
;     intro_seq $03A5 + cutscene_room $03ED + lz_unpack $008E = $0820  ->  $2000..$281F
;
; against a MEASURED LOADM ceiling of $2488..$2535 [link/pop_engine.link, P3.22] — over by
; $02EA..$0397. P3.104 stopped there and called it blocking.
;
; ★★★ JAY REFRAMED IT AND THAT IS WHAT THIS FILE IS: "D won't work since LOADM isn't
; available after initial load." LOADM is a BASIC command and BASIC is gone the moment the
; port takes control — so THE CEILING BINDS ON WHAT IS RESIDENT AT THE HANDOVER, NOT ON
; WHAT THE PROGRAM MAY EVER HOLD. The $820 was never too much code; it was too much code in
; the wrong stage.
;
; So the intro keeps the LOADM image ($2000..$2432, under the ceiling with room to spare)
; and the SCENE arrives afterwards, read from a whole track by the intro's own load_tracks
; over the kernel's disk_read_range — the route link/pop_engine.link already names: "put
; the code on a disk-resident track and reach it through a fixed table, the way the
; cutscene bundle does".
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY $2600, AND WHY BEING ABOVE THE CEILING IS THE POINT RATHER THAN A VIOLATION.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;   $2000..$2432   the intro's program — LOADM'd, and resident for the whole sequence
;   $2600..$2A7A   THIS, read from a track after the handover
;   $3000..$4883   the scene's flames bundle, expanded
;   $5400..$68F1   the intro's SAVE_BUF worst case (the TITLE caption, 5,361 B)
;   $5800..$69FF   the scene's packed bundle — see §3 of the P3.105 report for why those
;                  two overlap and are still safe
;   $6A00          DR_VARBASE      $6C00  peel buffers      $7800  trace      $7900  kernel
;
; $2600 clears the intro's code with 242 B of gap and clears $3000 by more than $500.
; ★ RAISED FROM $2500 AT P4.47: the intro prog grew past $2500 when BEAT_KEEP was added,
; and the scene's WHOLE-TRACK read from SCENE_BASE was clipping lz_unpack's tail.
; NOTHING LOADMs this image, so the ceiling does not apply to it — that is the whole
; mechanism, and stating it here is the point of the file.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE `code` SECTION IS DECLARED AND THEN DISCARDED, DELIBERATELY.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; cutscene_room.s calls HAL_sys_init, HAL_gfx_set_mode, HAL_gfx_mirror and
; HAL_time_frame_count. lwasm's object mode turns an undefined symbol into an external
; reference automatically, so the link needs hal_build.o present to RESOLVE them even
; though the kernel is already resident at $7900 from the intro's own LOADM.
;
; Declaring `code` at $7900 makes those references resolve to the addresses the resident
; kernel actually occupies. The build then drops that segment (decb_to_raw --span-end) so
; the track carries only $2600.. — because re-reading the kernel from a track WHILE THE
; KERNEL IS EXECUTING THE READ would overwrite the routine mid-transfer.
;
; ★ The two kernel images are byte-identical by construction: same build/obj/hal_build.o,
; same `code load 7900`. build.bat asserts it rather than trusting it
; (harness/tools/kernel_identical_check.py), because "identical by construction" is the
; shape of assumption this project has now been bitten by four times.
;
; Comments here are `;`. lwlink does NOT accept `*`, and a `$`-prefixed load value parses
; as ZERO with no error — both documented at length in link/pop_cels_res.link.

; ★★★ RAISED $2600 -> $2700 AT P5.16, AND THIS LINE IS A SECOND HOME FOR SCENE_BASE.
; build.bat says of SCENE_BASE that "Both assemblies take them from here so there is one
; home" -- and that is true of the two ASSEMBLIES and false of this LINK SCRIPT, which
; carries the address as a literal lwlink cannot take from a variable. P5.16 raised the
; constant in build.bat, left this at 2600, and the scene was LINKED at $2600 while being
; READ to $2700: every absolute address inside it off by $100. It ran far enough to issue
; its two preload reads and then died, with the drive still engaged, which looks nothing
; like "a link address is wrong".
; map_overlap_check.py now asserts scene.map loads exactly at SCENE_BASE, so the two homes
; cannot drift again without failing the build.
section prog load 2700
section code load 7900

entry room_entry
